(6406314, 948494, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: What a beautifully composed image. Great judgement of every element in the frame. The balance of the light is perfect too. Then there is the mixture of patterns of the surfaces and the strong diagonal lines across the frame. I haven''t even mentioned the figure yet - simultaneously important and irrelevant. I''m aware the image wouldn''t be the same without him but he doesn''t dominate the image.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Just the slight halo around the figure.<br/> <br/>Overall: One of those pictures that just hangs together.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: What a beautifully composed image. Great judgement of every element in the frame. The balance of the light is perfect too. Then there is the mixture of patterns of the surfaces and the strong diagonal lines across the frame. I haven''t even mentioned the figure yet - simultaneously important and irrelevant. I''m aware the image wouldn''t be the same without him but he doesn''t dominate the image. Critical stuff: Just the slight halo around the figure. Overall: One of those pictures that just hangs together.', '2011-05-07 04:08:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6406320, 948798, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: The blur is wonderful and prominent but it is the painting-like colours that grabs me here. Those colours and the light imbue the image with an Old Master / hanging in a public gallery feel. That suggestion carries over into the scene it self with my brain telling me the building behind is a gallery. The amount of detail you have preserved in many of the figures is just perfect, as is the degree of blur elsewhere.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing.<br/> <br/>Overall: Wonderfully made. The overall effect hits a number of sweet spots.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: The blur is wonderful and prominent but it is the painting-like colours that grabs me here. Those colours and the light imbue the image with an Old Master / hanging in a public gallery feel. That suggestion carries over into the scene it self with my brain telling me the building behind is a gallery. The amount of detail you have preserved in many of the figures is just perfect, as is the degree of blur elsewhere. Critical stuff: Nothing. Overall: Wonderfully made. The overall effect hits a number of sweet spots.', '2011-05-07 04:18:10.000000', NULL, 1),
