(6408231, 946497, 108580, '<td valign="top">Salut Julien. J''ai aimé l''image, et lui a donné un 7.<br/>Something about it made me feel it was "soft" perhaps the darkness of the overall image or the moving blurred clouds and water. Sure, cloud/water blur is unavoidable in timed exposures but I really felt it had translated into the pier and the mountains. In hindsight (recul?) I was probably wrong, the pier and mountains are indeed sharp.<br/>Regards, H</td>', 'Salut Julien. J''ai aimé l''image, et lui a donné un 7.Something about it made me feel it was "soft" perhaps the darkness of the overall image or the moving blurred clouds and water. Sure, cloud/water blur is unavoidable in timed exposures but I really felt it had translated into the pier and the mountains. In hindsight (recul?) I was probably wrong, the pier and mountains are indeed sharp.Regards, H', '2011-05-09 03:58:13.000000', NULL, 0),
