(6409101, 948046, 109387, '<td valign="top">Umbria is a wonderful region both for its history and its landscape - the cradle of arts and a great place for the ones who love mountains, waterfalls and caves. Which places have you visited there? I hope you''ve been to Castelluccio di Norcia, one of the best photographic places in the world. Each year in June and July people go there from all over the world to visit it. Its plateau, from an ancient glacial lake, is at 1200 metres a.s.l. and despite its altitude in those months is covered by a carpet of coloured flowers - an amazing view!<br/> <br/>Abruzzo is great because we have high mountains, wild places, lakes, green hills and a rich countryside and 200kms of coastline, all in a small region. A lot of places for a photographer.<br/> <br/>Ciao<br/>Alex</td>', 'Umbria is a wonderful region both for its history and its landscape - the cradle of arts and a great place for the ones who love mountains, waterfalls and caves. Which places have you visited there? I hope you''ve been to Castelluccio di Norcia, one of the best photographic places in the world. Each year in June and July people go there from all over the world to visit it. Its plateau, from an ancient glacial lake, is at 1200 metres a.s.l. and despite its altitude in those months is covered by a carpet of coloured flowers - an amazing view! Abruzzo is great because we have high mountains, wild places, lakes, green hills and a rich countryside and 200kms of coastline, all in a small region. A lot of places for a photographer. CiaoAlex', '2011-05-09 23:58:43.000000', NULL, 0),
